  "hybrid_observations": [
    "Actual two-Concat managed ggml region and checked Gather captured ranges plus a Prepared/nonblocking Store gap; warm PreferCapture reports Hybrid with real records.",
    "Public RequireCapture still rejects the incomplete capture coverage. Existing ranges restore via private reuse-only.",
    "Same-value marker in a different physical offset causes pure capture query, reuse preparation and pending bundle binding to reject; no recording or Commands fallback.",
    "Warm state/token/IDs guards are genuinely released; original blocks are reclaimed with same generation/resource/handle/offset/extent and original exact IDs carrier is rebound.",
    "A remains genuinely pending behind a host gate while B binds a token plus exact Store view from one original SubmissionSource; source count=1, device wait=1, host wait=0.",
    "B uses real Hybrid replay with recorded=0 and reused equal to the warm recorded range count. Its only original Completion is moved into a second SubmissionSource, also checking actual Hybrid producer admission.",
    "A retires while B is still gated, then detaches/takes/publishes/resets without overwriting B input. B produces exact token {2,7}, Store rows {3,5,7,11}; sentinel slots/padding remain unchanged and native uses return to zero."
  ],
  "append_observations": [
    "Independent block/domain/generation/epoch/exact committed+reserved tickets survive owner move, reject wrong or widened carriers, allocate no new budgeted bytes when copied, and expose no ready view.",
    "Real append admission now counts as a write, retaining original epoch-first error attribution. Ordered successors count as reads, so reader cancellation does not poison the append producer.",
    "Publication rejects before actual producer retirement; afterward exact publication succeeds with a readonly successor still pending. Public publish/reserve/rollback retain their original gates.",
    "Old ready prefix bounds never widen. New reserve invalidates prior epoch tickets; dropping tickets does not reopen writes in the sealed epoch.",
    "Producer failure rejects publication, waits for readonly successor retirement before rollback, and preserves old committed bytes. Closed domains reject new admission/publication but preserve pure identity queries."
  ],
  "implementation": [
    "A common cold range/gap classifier inspects original selected/runtime facts and actual submitted capture spans; no provider/op whitelist or new executor.",
    "Commands submissions inspect an empty capture partition, so dormant retained records cannot masquerade as actual launches.",
    "Ready-projection command retention is extended only to actual selected Operation readers with stable backend identity, no native inputs and the original preserves_capture_bindings proof; Region release contracts are unchanged."
  ],
  "not_verified_or_not_implemented": [
    "Append tests use controlled Completion protocol; no Graph KV append source or GPU KV dependency test in this batch.",
    "Fresh-page writer-to-appendable conversion, graph_batch export/bind, pending indexed GDN/conv readers and continuous bounded slot/COW rotation remain unimplemented.",
    "No complete Qwen/model overlap, MTP overlap, server API, multi-segment relay, new platform run, quality assessment or performance comparison.",
    "Source/bundle/replay preparation can still allocate cold metadata. No zero-allocation or tokens/s improvement is claimed.",
    "Hybrid failure propagation relies on existing whole-source regression cases; this new Hybrid case does not inject a GPU/driver failure."
  ],
